Z||000000||fldevel||11-19-2001||04:54 PM||||blew a hole in the radiator in my v-6 formula auto and was wandering if i could use the radiator from a 4-cyl auto ?? the radiators  "look" the same but was wandering if i could use the 4-cyl one .. <P> thanks,Dev||||reg||1
Z||000001||Pyric||11-19-2001||05:13 PM||||If it is from the same model year it should work.  The part number will hopefully match as well.  <P>The dealer only carries one radiator for each year regardless of whether its a 4 cylinder or a 6, so you should be safe.<P>if you want to see yourself checkout: <A HREF="http://www.auto-parts-for-less.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.auto-parts-for-less.com/</A> <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Pyric (edited 11-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||watts||11-19-2001||08:14 PM||||Not dead sure here, but from the ones that we've encountered around here - the V6's had one more core than the 4's.<P>You could also get one from Performance Radiators - they use one humungo core that's supposed to cool better than any of the factory ones.<BR><P>------------------<BR>87/88 V6 5spd Notchback Hybrid<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/watts_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
